{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic' pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_reap_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_subreaper_linux.go\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic' pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_reap_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_subreaper_linux.go\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:119:\t\tSummaryPtBR:     \"Executa a matriz determinística de validação em todos os módulos\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:149:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Realiza verificação estrutural completa em todos os arquivos do POSE, links quebrados em markdown, sintaxe de frontmatter, schemas JSON e grafos de specs.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:190:\t\tSummaryPtBR:     \"Lista, filtra e descobre especificações em todo o repositório\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:328:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"pose review governa o sujeito (bundle, brief, atestação, verify); pose delegate governa as execuções. Termos: um agente é um perfil de CLI configurado em .pose/policy/delegation.json; um run é uma execução; uma tentativa é um run e suas continuações; uma thread são as rodadas de um escopo. review, adjudicate e smoke rodam o brief gerado do bundle selado num worktree descartável no commit selado, só com acesso de leitura, sob o ledger de tentativas e a contenção. Com delegated-review adotado e conclusions.issuer configurado, o motor registra automaticamente a conclusão completa e verificada; processo concluído sozinho nunca aprova. Sem --agent (ou com auto) o roteamento escolhe um agente do propósito: o vendor oposto ao da implementação que o bundle selou (routing.prefer), depois routing.on_unavailable (outro modelo do mesmo vendor, esperar um reset conhecido dentro de routing.max_wait, o mesmo modelo); --agent <nome> dispensa o roteamento e avisa quando o agente é do vendor da implementação. Todo run registra a decisão de roteamento e a independência alcançada. O processo filho não recebe nenhuma variável de sessão do agente pai. --dry-run mostra agente, propósito, acesso, diretório de trabalho e argv resolvidos e não reserva nada; --json imprime um documento versionado. Uma referência de run é um id de run, um id de tentativa, um --label ou um prefixo de sessão com seis caracteres ou mais. --detach inicia o run numa sessão própria e devolve a tentativa na hora; wait bloqueia até um run terminar e sai com 0 aprovado, 10 mudanças pedidas ou rejeitado, 20 falhou, 30 interrompido, 40 travado, 50 tempo esgotado. watch acompanha um run ao vivo, reproduzindo uma tentativa retomada como uma tarefa só, e escolhe um run com fzf ou um menu num terminal; on_terminal roda um comando uma vez depois que um run termina. handoff continua um run parado com outro agente na mesma tentativa; task entrega uma tarefa geral a outro agente, nunca como evidência; wait sai com 0 quando o agente teve sucesso. pose review dispatch, resume e status foram removidos. As mensagens seguem POSE_LOCALE.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:386:\t\t\t{\"draft-check\", \"pose review draft-check [<bundle-id|run-id>] --draft <file> [--json]\", \"Report every reason the conclusion step would refuse a review draft, without writing; inside a delegated review the bundle and round come from the run\", \"Relata todo motivo pelo qual a conclusão recusaria um rascunho de review, sem gravar; dentro de uma review delegada o bundle e a rodada vêm do run\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:577:\t\t\t{\"list\", \"pose contribute list [--json]\", \"List all staged contributions awaiting developer adjudication\", \"Lista todos os rascunhos locais aguardando avaliação do desenvolvedor\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:633:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Agrega todos os follow-ups declarados nas specs na seção 7 (Final Report), sinalizando SLAs vencidos e propostas quase-duplicadas.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:636:\t\t\t{\"--all\", \"List all follow-ups across all specs regardless of disposition\", \"Lista todos os follow-ups em todas as specs independentemente da disposição\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:651:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Recalcula e grava todos os índices estáticos incluindo spec-graph.json, roadmaps.json, releases.json e delivery-integrity.json, como uma geração confirmada por .pose/indexes/generation.json.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:725:\t\t\t{\"tech-debt\", \"pose assess tech-debt [--update-state] [--no-persist]\", \"Scan codebase for technical debt markers and uncovered stubs\", \"Escaneia a base de código por marcadores de débito e stubs\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:803:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Verifica se todos os arquivos declarados na seção 3 (Technical Plan -> Artifacts) correspondem ao changeset real do Git atribuído via trailer (POSE-Spec: <slug>).\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:884:\t\t\t{\"--outcomes\", \"Governance: with --waits/--rework, also compute the outcomes (reads the whole history)\", \"Governance: com --waits/--rework, calcula também os resultados (lê todo o histórico)\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:948:\t\tSummaryPtBR:     \"Verifica se todos os arquivos de log histórico estão rastreados no Git\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:951:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Garante que todos os arquivos históricos de tarefas sob .pose/reports/history/ estejam commitados e rastreados no controle de versão.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:429:\t\t\"pose delegate: todos os agentes anteriores estão limitados; esperando até \"+record.WaitUntil+\" para iniciar \"+agent))\npose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:535:\t\t\t\t\"todos os agentes estão limitados até \"+route.WaitUntil+\"; um run destacado não espera um reset: rode sem --detach, ou depois do reset\")))\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:204:\tplan.OnStart = func(a string) error { attempt = a; panic(\"the dispatching process ends here\") }\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:277:\tplan.OnStart = func(a string) error { attempt = a; panic(\"the dispatching process ends here\") }\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go:427:\tbeforeRunResultPublished = func(r ReviewRun) { recorded = r.RunID; panic(\"the dispatching process ends before the receipt\") }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_DRAFT_EOF' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\n      \"line\": 1027,\n      \"summary\": \"If PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER fails, the error is discarded and cleanup continues without the orphan scan. An escaped descendant that cleared POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT can survive while the run still completes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\n      \"line\": 1028,\n      \"summary\": \"reviewClockTicks errors are ignored, leaving adapterSince at zero. The orphan scan can then treat pre-existing adopted children as run orphans and SIGKILL processes outside this run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 110,\n      \"summary\": \"A processStartTime error is ignored and stores an empty start value; an absent baseline entry also reads as empty, so an opaque process started during this run can be counted as pre-existing. review_subreaper_linux.go:102-104 also skips unreadable stat errors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N4\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 68,\n      \"summary\": \"The reviewer-controlled /proc/PID/comm name is copied raw into safety.limitations and persisted by review_dispatch.go:1059, bypassing the credential redaction applied to captured output.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R6-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\"'AnOrphanThatCleared|NonInspectable|UnreadableMarker|InterruptedDispatchIsReleased|MarkerlessReservation|RecordedRunCompletes|OneReleaseRuns'; delegation_release.go:201-205\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R6-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'AnOrphanThatCleared|NonInspectable|UnreadableMarker|InterruptedDispatchIsReleased|MarkerlessReservation|RecordedRunCompletes|OneReleaseRuns'; review_reap_linux_test.go:98-120\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R6-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'AnOrphanThatCleared|NonInspectable|UnreadableMarker|InterruptedDispatchIsReleased|MarkerlessReservation|RecordedRunCompletes|OneReleaseRuns'; review_reap_linux_test.go:81-94\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed all 22 files in the supplied change list: process cleanup on Linux and other platforms, subreaper setup and scanning, dispatch ordering and cleanup inventory, attempt ledger/release/list/cancel, CLI/help, brief rendering and immutable digests, tests, and root/Portuguese manual and scaffold copies. Rechecked all three R6 findings and searched .pose/knowledge for relevant process-cleanup and delegated-review decisions.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified: the adapter environment adds the run checkout marker, marked PIDs are checked again before pidfd signaling, and marker-backed release requires a proven-dead owner. Unresolved: subreaper and /proc uptime failures are ignored (N1, N2), and unreadable process start metadata can be treated as pre-existing (N3). Accepted spec limits remain L1, L2, L4 and L5.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The release lock and dead-owner checks are covered by focused tests, but unreadable process metadata can be treated as absence during cleanup, so lifecycle completion is not safe on that error path.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel option is additive, existing record schemas are unchanged, and released attempts use ordinary failed-run and receipt records.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The failure of PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER is silently converted into a disabled orphan scan, with no typed refusal or cleanup failure.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change stays within the pose-mcp CLI and domain cleanup path; no public REST, Protobuf, Kafka or MCP contract changed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The termination record persists an untrusted process name without applying the credential redaction used for captured output.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new cancel flag and failed-run receipt are additive, and earlier record formats retain their meaning.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"On a Linux host where subreaper setup fails, an environment-cleared descendant outside the process group is not found, yet the no-match scan can permit a completed run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses the process-group escape with the checkout marker and a subreaper; D2 preserves abandoned attempts through failed-run records and receipts. The structural design assessment emitted no deltas. The unchecked clock failure can widen the subreaper scan beyond this run, so the chosen ownership boundary is not upheld on that path.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The current review-brief/10 asks commands to finish, and the root, locale and scaffold manuals describe Linux cleanup, non-Linux limits and abandoned-attempt release.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"When subreaper setup fails, the run does not explain that escaped-process cleanup is unavailable and may still conclude.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1/R2 depend on cleanup completing before inventory and recording ended processes; the failed-subreeaper path can leave a process running without making the run incomplete.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The supplied subject changes review dispatch cleanup, abandoned-attempt recovery, the CLI/help, review brief and its manual/scaffold copies as declared by the spec.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A reviewer-controlled process name can carry a short credential into a persisted run record and CLI output without redaction; the unchecked start-time boundary also risks signaling an unrelated process (N2).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Group-only cleanup is insufficient for commands started in their own session, so the checkout marker and subreaper address the stated cause. The process-wide subreaper risk L5 is explicit, but an unreadable cutoff currently expands selection to pre-existing children, beyond that accepted limit.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exited 0. It printed repository-wide orphan warnings and a broader slug lineage; the supplied range and listed subject paths were reviewed directly.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-8127b147a553e24d\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the assessment; it reported status observed and no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence and discovered pose-mcp.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence; the three unobserved HTTP declarations are outside the changed cleanup and CLI contracts.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran, but the scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs have invalid/unknown scope and it reported one uncovered marker; the changed production diff has no TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker, while the observed panic calls are test seams that simulate interruption.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran; this completion-only check refused because the spec is not done and there is no approved review attestation, which this brief prohibits recording.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran; deferred because it requires a completed review attestation. It also reported that local semantic inputs are not represented by its selected sealed bundle.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules for this component.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results and zero findings.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran strict validation; Go checks could not create their build/cache paths in this read-only sandbox. The sealed build, e2e, integration and unit results cover the module, and focused review tests and vet passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran strict module validation; Go checks could not create build/cache paths in this read-only sandbox. The sealed component build and unit results remain available, and focused review tests and vet passed.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_DRAFT_EOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
